Falsifies `capability::subset_is_reflexive`.

The defect: the negation dropped from `is_subset_of`, `self.0 & other.0` instead of
`self.0 & !other.0`. A missing `!` is an ordinary typo and the compiler cannot see it,
since both spellings are `u32 & u32 == 0`.

Expected to fail: `assert!(a.is_subset_of(a))`, for any `a` with a bit set.

**This record is honest about being weak, and that is why it is worth having.** It is
the tree's clearest tautology: it proves `a & !a == 0`. The
patch above does turn it red, so it is not decorative, but every mutation of
`is_subset_of` that reaches this harness also reaches `subset_matches_allows` and
`derive_never_widens_rights`, while the reverse is false (see
subset_matches_allows.patch, which this harness survives). A harness whose falsification
set is a strict subset of another's adds no discrimination to the suite. Nothing here
proposes deleting it; the record is what lets somebody argue about that with evidence.

diff --git a/crates/capability/src/lib.rs b/crates/capability/src/lib.rs
index 33b5819a..27660f5e 100644
--- a/crates/capability/src/lib.rs
+++ b/crates/capability/src/lib.rs
@@ -140,7 +140,7 @@ impl Rights {
 
     /// Is `self` no more than `other`? The subset test that [`CapabilityTable::derive`] turns on.
     pub const fn is_subset_of(self, other: Rights) -> bool {
-        self.0 & !other.0 == 0
+        self.0 & other.0 == 0
     }
 }
 
